{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Architecture Styles"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear and use to talk about architecture styles. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Build the application installation program, using IT development tools available in the market, based on solution architecture features.  Recognizes and implements the different types of architecture styles that can be included in the IT solution."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.  Exchanges simple information on the hardware devices and the architecture of a system to create the IT solution."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pipe   "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "means of transport for data"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: A pipe is the connection that carries the data to the filters."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob07aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "filter "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "component with a set of inputs and outputs "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Filters might have parameters to perform this action."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob07aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "stream "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a flow of components "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: A filter is structured to read a stream of a data as input and produce output."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob07aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "conduit"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "where components travel through to get from one filter to another"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It serves as a conduit of outputs that become inputs once they're delivered to the filter."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob07aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "throughput "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "quantity of processes within a specific time"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They may use reusable components that communicate with one another and build a constant throughput."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob07aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "deadlock  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a stage where a process is not able to continue"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We may establish objectives and restrictions, so, we don't fall in a deadlock."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob07aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "a)\tLook for information about architecture styles"}, {"type": "text", "content": "b)\tTakes notes about those architecture styles"}, {"type": "text", "content": "c)\tMake a chart where you write a little description of each architecture style."}, {"type": "text", "content": "d)\tUse the information in the chart to create a brochure to promote the style that somebody could use."}, {"type": "text", "content": "e)\tShare your brochure with your partners. "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "\u274f\tI search information about architecture style. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "\u274f\tI describe each architecture style."}, {"type": "text", "content": "\u274f\tI express what style could be the best option to use in a system. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "\u274f\tI share with my partners. "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Modal verbs for speculating- might/ may."}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the modal verbs <span class=\"strong\"> might  </span> and <span class=\"strong\"> may  </span> to create statements for speculating about any topic."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The modal verbs <span class=\"strong\"> may  </span> and <span class=\"strong\"> might  </span> besides expressing probability, they are used to speculate about procedures or reactions. <br/> <br/> Let's check the grammatical structure: <br/><br/> Subject + <span class=\"strong\"> may/might  </span> + verb (base form) + complement. <br/><br/> Example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\"> Software architectures <span class=\"strong\"> may  </span> include useful data structures. <br/> Architectural descriptions <span class=\"strong\"> might  </span> be part of the style definition. </span> <br/><br/>  Although <span class=\"strong\"> may  </span> and <span class=\"strong\"> might  </span> are very similar in meaning, their difference lays on the intention of the message. If you use <span class=\"strong\"> may  </span> in a statement, it is because you are surer about it than if you use <span class=\"strong\"> might </span>, because, in the latter case, you are less sure about the situation."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Filters might have parameters to perform this action."}, {"type": "example", "content": "We may establish objectives and restrictions, so, we don't fall in a deadlock."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You may need to verify features such as inheritance, encapsulation, abstraction, and polymorphism."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Architecture styles Summary."}, {"type": "describer", "content": "The structure of any system formed by software components is called <span class=\"strong\"> architecture </span>. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "An architectural style determines the vocabulary that is going to be used for the components and the connectors within a system. There are different architectural styles that define how a particular system is designed. So far, there is not a global taxonomy to develop software architectures, instead there are several individual ways to create them.  <br/><br/> Now, we are going to check some of the most common styles where architecture is represented."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Architecture styles are patterns or frameworks for software development. They are designed to solve difficulties when structuring a program."}, {"type": "example", "content": "These styles are implemented to define the relation among the components that will be part of the system."}, {"type": "example", "content": "There's another architecture style that I like. It is called object-oriented and it's about breaking down a system into individual parts."}], "type": "learning_points"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n6le01ob07re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe8n6le01ob07re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Sara:</span> Hey Drake, what are you reading? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Drake:</span> It's a book I got to learn about architecture styles, I have to design an application as part of a project in my engineering class. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Sara:</span> Cool! What have you learned about architecture styles so far? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Drake:</span> Architecture styles are patterns or frameworks for software development. They are designed to solve difficulties when structuring a program. These styles are implemented to define the relation among the components that will be a part of the system. They are very important because we may establish objectives and restrictions, so, we don't fall in a deadlock."}, {"time": "39500", "image": "enpe8n6le01ob07re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Sara:</span> And what style are you going to use? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Drake:</span> There's one called pipes and filters, it's very simple. A filter is structured to read a stream of data as input and produce output, filters might have parameters to perform this action. A pipe is the connection that carries the data to the filters; it serves as a conduit of outputs that become inputs once they're delivered to the filter. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Sara:</span> You might know a lot about software to implement something like that."}, {"time": "71500", "image": "enpe8n6le01ob07re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Drake:</span> Yes, I'm very interested in these concepts. Actually, there's another architecture style that I like. It is called object-oriented and it's about breaking down a system into individual parts. They may use reusable components that communicate with one another and build a constant throughput by sending and receiving messages. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Sara:</span> Well, you might take into account that not all systems can be broken down into defined objects. I worked on a similar project where I used the object-oriented style, and you may need to verify features such as inheritance, encapsulation, abstraction, and polymorphism. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Drake:</span> Wow, I didn't expect you to know about this topic. Would you help me understand some concepts? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Sara:</span> Sure!"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n6le01ob07re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}, {"template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "static", "_data": [], "id": 2, "contents": [{"value": "Escalera 1.jpg", "type": "img"}, {"value": "Escalera 2.jpg", "type": "img"}, {"value": "Escalera 3.jpg", "type": "img"}, {"value": "Escalera 4.jpg", "type": "img"}]}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about architecture styles."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can describe the pipes and filters architecture style."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can explain the object-oriented style."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What types of architecture styles do you know about?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What aspects would you take into account to design your own application?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Different Ways to Compose a System "}], "img_path": "", "id": 0}, {"stimuli_ids": [1], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "type": "question"}], "responses": [{"correct": 0, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0}, {"correct": 1, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 1}], "id": 0}], "type": "ST